```

## Verify (CI gate)

```bash
genesis verify   # exit 2 while any hole remains
```

Wire `genesis verify` into CI so unfilled logic cannot ship. It fails while ANY of these hold:

- a `GenesisTODO.notImplemented` marker remains in `Sources/` (unfilled domain hole),
- a declared aggregate invariant has no **enabled live-assertion** test (a `.<code>` token inside a thunk message or comment does NOT count as coverage),
- a `genesisTODO(...)` arrange-thunk remains in an enabled `@Test` (unfilled test-side Given).

`genesis verify` is RED throughout development and green only when all three are clear. A green `verify` with a still-red `swift test` means the Given is semantically wrong or localhost KurrentDB is down — not an unfilled hole.

